From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 03:54:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ad5x: setup wizard filament step, live progress, Z offset
 plan, prompts
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

What a fresh install showed: the Z offset step didn't say which slot,
material or temperatures it would print with; a long step showed one
static line and a thin bar; and after the Z offset nothing said to take
the test print off the bed before the next step probed there.

New step Filament (StepId::Ad5xFilament, Klipper's STEP=filament),
between vibration compensation and IFS tuning. It lists the four IFS
slots from printer.ad5x_setup.filament: a material dropdown for each
slot with filament (Unknown, then the IFS's types from
AmsBackendAd5xIfs::kStockWhitelist, plus the slot's own type when it is
another one), "Empty" for the others; and "Filament in the toolhead":
Auto (find it), Slot 1-4, None (empty), Use the filament in the toolhead
as it is (keep, e.g. hand-fed). The dropdowns follow the live object
until the user changes one. Start sends head (auto, 1-4, 0, keep) and
material_<n> for each slot the user changed ("?" for Unknown). The
toolhead choices are one table (head_choices()). A line under it says
what the toolhead holds now (also "kept as it is" and "strand in the
tube, slot unknown"); the IFS and Z offset pages show it too before
Start. When printer.ifs.tube_blocked is set (or head_source is tube),
the filament page warns: a strand is still in the tube, name the slot
first. The step reads tube_blocked, find_result, head_found and colors
of printer.ifs (queried with ad5x_setup, and taken from its updates).

Every running AD5X step shows, besides the message and progress bar:
the action key as a short phrase ("Probing the bed", "Loading slot 2",
"Printing test patch 2"; an unknown key as it is), and once a second
the nozzle and bed temperature with their targets and the time since
step_started. When the printer clock is not set (1970 before NTP, or
far from the screen's time), the screen counts from when it first saw
the run.

Z offset: from the start, the patch's plan from zoffset_plan ("Slot 2,
PETG, 240/70 C"); with guess set it says PLA's temperatures are used and
to Abort and set the material in the Filament step if that is wrong.

Prompts: clear_bed while waiting shows "Remove the test print from the
bed" with Done (accept) and hides the adjust buttons, the live view and
Abort; after a failed or aborted Z offset a reminder to clear the bed
with Done (accept clears it there too). head_unknown shows how to pull
the filament out by hand before Retry. pick_slot (failed: Kiln can't
tell the slot on this printer, or a strand sits in the tube) asks which
slot's filament goes into the toolhead: a button per slot with filament
(all four when none is known), "Slot 2 · PETG" with the spool's colour
from printer.ifs.colors, and "I pulled it out by hand". A slot runs the
filament step with head=<n>, "by hand" with head=0; from the IFS or Z
offset card that filament run shows on the card, which then offers its
own Start again. Retry before naming asks again. A prompt key the screen
doesn't know shows the step's message with Done (accept) while waiting,
Retry when failed.

The G-code fallback sends string options unquoted (HEAD=auto).

Tests: test_wizard_ad5x_setup.cpp (phrases, elapsed time and the clock
guard, temperatures, the filament object, material choices, start
options with keep, the plan, prompts with pick_slot, the pick buttons'
labels, the printer.ifs fields, step order; the filament card loads
from XML with its dropdowns, the clear_bed panel hides the adjust
buttons and the pick_slot panel names each slot);
test_wizard_step_logic counts the new step.
